+/// its last statement), a `Function`, and a `Method` (a call returns it).
+/// Every other block — an `if` branch, a loop body, a `try` body, a module —
+/// is a statement, and a statement consumes what it produced.
+///
+/// That distinction is not an optimisation. `if 1 is 1 then 7 end` is worth
+/// `nothing` on the tree-walking VM, and a compile that treated every block
